  "worker_judgment_notes": "Official City of Orlando OPD Records & Open Data links the public Crime & Cases Dashboard; the dashboard web map resolves to the public OPD_Cases_Viewing FeatureServer point layer with OBJECTID, CaseNumber, CaseDate, CaseType/GISCaseType, NeighborhoodName, ORI, and point geometry. The contract is share-lane only: raw feed rows are not promoted as annual totals. jurisdiction_id/state_fips come from state/controls/jurisdiction_controls_2024.parquet for Orlando city. Bounds use the local TIGER/crosswalk Orlando municipal block-group extent so the runner can spatially join municipal block groups; the official Orlando city-limits layer was also checked and is slightly narrower eastward. Offense mapping is strict and offense-selective: Homicide maps to murder while Vehicular Homicide is excluded; robbery uses OPD robbery/carjacking categories; aggravated_assault uses Aggravated Assault, Aggravated Battery, and Attempted Homicide while simple Assault, Battery, Battery on LEO/Firefighter, weapons, and shooting-at-structure categories are excluded; burglary excludes Vehicle Burglary, which is treated as larceny; larceny excludes fraud, identity theft, embezzlement, recovered/found/lost property, and dealing-in-stolen-property noise; motor_vehicle_theft includes completed and attempted motor vehicle theft but excludes recovered stolen vehicles. No defendable rape/sex-offense category was exposed in the public GISCaseType list or definition table, so rape is intentionally omitted. ArcGIS JSON date values are epoch milliseconds; CaseDate is the source date field, and an ingestion runner should normalize ArcGIS date fields accordingly.",
